stakes thereof shall ever be removed, neither shall any of the cords thereof be broken.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙŸBut there the glorious LORD will be unto us a place of broad rivers and streams; wherein shall go no galley with oars, neither shall gallant ship pass thereby.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ[For the LORD is our judge, the LORD is our lawgiver, the LORD is our king; he will save us.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter!«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses’„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ§Thy tacklings are loosed; they could not well strengthen their mast, they could not spread the sail: then is the prey of a great spoil divided; the lame take the prey.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙlAnd the inhabitant shall not say, I am sick: the people that dwell therein shall be forgiven their iniquity.¦layout ªlast_verse